From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:38:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8781-zinwa-q25: Keep the bootloader's
 display alive

The bootloader leaves the DISP power domain and the display pipeline
clocks running for the framebuffer it scans out. Nothing in Linux
claimed them, so genpd and the clock framework would switch them off
as unused and the screen went dark; the board needed pd_ignore_unused
and clk_ignore_unused.

List the DISP domain and the clocks of the OVL0 -> RDMA0 -> COLOR0 ->
CCORR0 -> AAL0 -> GAMMA0 -> POSTMASK0 -> DITHER0 -> DSI0 path on the
simple-framebuffer node, which simpledrm holds until a display driver
takes over, as linux-mediatek's mt6789-xiaomi-emerald does for the
domain (ec1b71bd3149, "emerald: Fix random simplefb crashes").

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
index 104c65a2..7cd6ce07 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8781-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -59,6 +59,20 @@
 			height = <720>;
 			stride = <(736 * 4)>;
 			format = "a8r8g8b8";
+			power-domains = <&spm MT6789_POWER_DOMAIN_DISP>;
+			clocks = <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_MUTEX0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_APB_BUS>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_OVL0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_RDMA0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_COLOR0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_CCORR0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_AAL0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_GAMMA0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_POSTMASK0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_DITHER0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DSI0>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DSI0_DSI_CK_DOMAIN>,
+				 <&mmsys CLK_MM_DISP_26M>;
 		};
 	};
 
